      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t_mechanism",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 530,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 86,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1754092800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THE MECHANISM SHIFT\nAn app-embedded cache only ever sees its own process's requests — it has no way to know a hundred other pods just\nmissed the exact same entity. A cache living in the mesh sees every caller's request pass through the same layer,\nso it can hold back duplicates and let one fetch answer for all of them.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THE MECHANISM SHIFT\nAn app-embedded cache only ever sees its own process's requests — it has no way to know a hundred other pods just\nmissed the exact same entity. A cache living in the mesh sees every caller's request pass through the same layer,\nso it can hold back duplicates and let one fetch answer for all of them.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "b_numbers",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 648,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#3730a3",
      "backgroundColor": "#eef2ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [{ "id": "t_numbers", "type": "text" }],
      "updated": 1754092800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "t_numbers",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 660,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 76,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1754092800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHAT THE VANTAGE POINT BOUGHT\n1.5M+ requests/sec across 100+ endpoints, 50 services. 90%+ hit rate on the busiest endpoints. ~5x per-pod\nthroughput. P99 latency spikes cut up to 80%. Kafka timestamp-comparison invalidation — no cross-pod delete\ncoordination, correct even out of order.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WHAT THE VANTAGE POINT BOUGHT\n1.5M+ requests/sec across 100+ endpoints, 50 services. 90%+ hit rate on the busiest endpoints. ~5x per-pod\nthroughput. P99 latency spikes cut up to 80%. Kafka timestamp-comparison invalidation — no cross-pod delete\ncoordination, correct even out of order.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_footnote",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 768,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#0f766e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1754092800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "No one was wrong. Per-service caching does cut a process's own repeat calls — it just can't see what every\nother pod is asking for at the same instant. The tradeoff didn't disappear when DoorDash moved caching into\nthe mesh. It moved to whoever forgets to publish a Kafka event.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "No one was wrong. Per-service caching does cut a process's own repeat calls — it just can't see what every\nother pod is asking for at the same instant. The tradeoff didn't disappear when DoorDash moved caching into\nthe mesh. It moved to whoever forgets to publish a Kafka event.",
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    }
  ],
